ENTRY            32914   20241015   20261124   20261124       3224
SUBENT        32914001   20241015   20261124   20261124       3224
BIB                 12         44
TITLE      New experimental measurement of natSe(n,g) cross
            section between 1 eV to 1keV at the CSNS Back-n
            facility
AUTHOR     (Xin-Rong Hu, Long-Xiang Liu, Wei Jiang, Jie Ren,
            Gong-Tao Fan, Hong-Wei Wang, Xi-Guang Cao,
            Long-Long Song, Ying-Du Liu, Yue Zhang, Xin-Xiang Li,
            Zi-Rui Hao, Pan Kuang, Xiao-He Wang, Ji-Feng Hu,
            Bing Jiang, De-Xin Wang, Suyalatu Zhang, Zhen-Dong An,
            Yu-Ting Wang, Chun-Wang Ma, Jian-Jun He, Jun Su,
            Li-Yong Zhang, Yu-Xuan Yang, Sheng Jin, Kai-Jie Chen)
INSTITUTE  (3CPRNRS,3CPRUCA,3CPRARI,3CPRIHP,3CPRAEP,3CPRSZH,
            3CPRBNU,3CPRZHN,3CPRSST)
           (3CPRCPR) Xiangtan University, Xiangtan; Inner
            Mongolia University for the Nationalities, Tongliao;
            Henan Normal University, Xinxiang
REFERENCE  (J,CPH/B,31,080101,2022)
           #doi:10.1088/1674-1056/ac6ee2
FACILITY   (SYNCH,3CPRIHP) The neutron time-of-flight facility
            Back-n is one of the neutron beam lines in China
            Spallation Neutron Source (CSNS)
INC-SOURCE (SPALL) Neutrons are produced by a pulse proton beam
            with an energy of 1.6 GeV and a repetition frequency
            of 25 Hz, bombarding a tungsten-tantalum (W-CTa)
            target.
SAMPLE     The natural Se sample consisted of selenium monomers
            in powder form with a purity of 99.99%. Its mass is
            18.89+-0.02 g, diameter is 50+-1 mm, thickness is
            2.00+-0.02 mm and area density is 7.304E-3 atom/barn.
DETECTOR   (SCIN) Four deuterated benzene (C6D6) liquid
            scintillator detectors were used for the gamma-ray
            detection. The shell of the scintillator is made of
            aluminum due to its low capture rate, with a diameter
            and length of 130 mm and 76.2 mm, respectively. The
            distance between the detector center to the sample
            centre is about 150 mm, and the distance from the
            neutron beam centre to the centre of the front face
            of the detector is about 80 mm.
           (SILI) The neutron flux was measured by a Li-Si
            detector, which is based on the 6Li(n,a) 3H reaction.
METHOD     (TOF,PHWT) Flight distance is 76 m
CORRECTION Corrected for neutron multiple scattering with GEANT4
ANALYSIS   The experimental capture yield was normalized by the
            saturated resonance method with Au 4.9 eV resonance.
HISTORY    (20241014C) Yang Su (CNDC)
ENDBIB              44
NOCOMMON             0          0
ENDSUBENT           47
SUBENT        32914002   20241015   20261124   20261124       3224
BIB                  4         10
REACTION   (34-SE-0(N,G),,SIG)
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S) Statistic uncertainty
           (ERR-1,,8.0) The uncertainty of the neutron energy
            spectrum varies between 2.3% and 4.5% above 0.15 MeV
            and less than 8.0% below 0.15 MeV.
           (ERR-2,,3.5) Uncertainty of proton beam power
           (ERR-3,2.0,3.0) Uncertainty from PHWT
           (ERR-4) Uncertainty of normalization
STATUS     (TABLE,,Xin-Rong Hu+,J,CPH/C,31,038101,2022)
HISTORY    (20240923R) The data received from Xin-Rong Hu
ENDBIB              10
COMMON               1          3
ERR-4
PER-CENT
        1.0
ENDCOMMON            3
